section.kbd:
fn:items-after(
         $input	as item()*,	
         $predicate	as function(item()) as xs:boolean	
         ) as item()*

fn:items-before(
         $input	as item()*,	
         $predicate	as function(item()) as xs:boolean	
         ) as item()*

fn:items-ending-where(
         $input	as item()*,	
         $predicate	as function(item()) as xs:boolean	
         ) as item()*

fn:items-starting-where(
         $input	as item()*,	
         $predicate	as function(item()) as xs:boolean	
         ) as item()*

section.aside:
This syntax is available from Saxon 12.3. The previous proposal ->($a, $b){$a + $b}
         remains available for the time being. The new form does not allow argument types and return types to
         be declared.
